@startuml
title User Service - Deactivate and Reactivate Account

autonumber
hide footbox
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor Client
boundary "Users Router\napp/routes/users.py" as API
control "Authentication\napp/auth.py" as Auth
control "User Operations\napp/services/users.py" as Users

== Deactivate account ==

Client -> API: DELETE /users/me or\nPOST /users/me/deactivate\nBearer token
activate API

ref over API, Auth
  Authenticate request
  See authorizeProtectedRequest.puml
end ref

alt Authentication fails
  API --> Client: 401 Unauthorized
else Request is authenticated
  API -> Users: deactivate_user(authenticated user)
  activate Users

  alt Account is no longer active
    Users --> API: Deactivation rejected
    API --> Client: 401 Unauthorized
  else Deactivation succeeds
    Users -> Auth: revoke_user_sessions(user id)
    activate Auth
    Auth --> Users: Sessions revoked
    deactivate Auth
    Users --> API: Deactivated user
    API --> Client: 200 OK + deactivated profile
  else Service unavailable
    Users --> API: Operation unavailable
    API --> Client: 503 Service Unavailable
  end
  deactivate Users
end
deactivate API

== Reactivate account ==

Client -> API: POST /users/reactivate (or alias)\nStudent number + password
activate API

alt Invalid request format
  API --> Client: 422 Validation error
else Valid request format
  API -> Users: reactivate_user(credentials)
  activate Users

  alt Unknown user, wrong password, or suspended account
    Users --> API: Reactivation rejected
    API --> Client: 401 Invalid credentials
  else Credentials accepted
    note right of Users
      The existing account is reactivated.
      Revoked sessions are not restored and
      no new token is issued.
    end note
    Users --> API: Active user
    API --> Client: 200 OK + active profile
  else Service unavailable
    Users --> API: Operation unavailable
    API --> Client: 503 Service Unavailable
  end
  deactivate Users
end

deactivate API
@enduml
